---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Toc from '../components/Toc.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const toc = [
	{id: 'security-report', label: 'SecurityReport'},
	{id: 'report-id', label: 'reportId'},
	{id: 'evidence', label: 'Execution evidence'},
	{id: 'export', label: 'Export policy'},
	{id: 'ci', label: 'CI semantics'},
];
---

<DocsLayout
	title="Reports"
	eyebrow="[ 07 · EVIDENCE ]"
	description="One SecurityReport object — two export formats that always agree, with collision-safe writes."
>
	<Toc items={toc} />

	<h2 id="security-report">SecurityReport</h2>
	<p>
		Canonical schema <code>schemaVersion: "1.0.0"</code>. Built from an
		<code>AuditRun</code> (scan + ChaosReport) by <code>security_report.ts</code>. Full field
		map and sample JSON → <a href={withBase('/report-schema')}>Report schema</a>.
	</p>

	<ul>
		<li>Target info (contract, network, bytecode size)</li>
		<li>Scan summary (functions / UDTs)</li>
		<li>Findings with signal, severity, KYF IDs</li>
		<li>Severity / signal counts</li>
		<li>Execution evidence (below)</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="report-id">reportId</h2>
	<p>
		Generated by <code>generateReportId()</code>:
		<code>kyf-&lt;ISO-stamp&gt;-&lt;8 uuid chars&gt;</code>.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Not derived from Contract ID alone — two audits of the same contract get distinct IDs.</li>
		<li>Filename-safe by construction; export still sanitizes non <code>[A-Za-z0-9._-]</code>.</li>
		<li>
			Headless <code>--json --pdf</code>: one shared <code>buildSecurityReport()</code>
			call → identical <code>reportId</code> in both files.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="evidence">Execution evidence</h2>
	<p>So claims can be checked without trusting Kuyfi’s own word:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Run-wide counters: vectors executed, <code>broadcastTransactions</code>,
			<code>transactionsWithHash</code> — counted across <strong>all</strong> vector
			results, not only the filtered findings list.
		</li>
		<li>
			Per finding: simulation failed?, broadcast?, parsed DiagnosticEvent trace.
		</li>
		<li>
			If broadcast: <code>transactionHash</code>, <code>ledger</code>, explorer URL
			<code>https://stellar.expert/explorer/testnet/tx/&lt;hash&gt;</code>.
		</li>
		<li>
			<code>verificationTransactions</code>: deterministic sample of at most
			<strong>two</strong> entries — first successful broadcast with hash, and first
			failed broadcast with hash. Empty if nothing was broadcast. Not a full dump.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<Callout type="info" title="Not every finding has a tx">
		<p>
			Simulation failures are classified from diagnostics and never sent. Only broadcast
			transactions can be independently verified on-chain. Note:
			<code>InvokeResult.broadcasted</code> can be false while a local envelope hash
			still exists (<code>SEND_ERROR</code>) — always check both fields.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2 id="export">Export policy</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Format</th>
				<th>How</th>
				<th>Notes</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td>JSON</td>
				<td>TUI <code>[J]</code> / CLI <code>--json</code></td>
				<td><code>kuyfi-report-&lt;reportId&gt;.json</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>PDF</td>
				<td>TUI <code>[P]</code> / CLI <code>--pdf</code></td>
				<td>
					pdfkit; labeled as automated black-box, not a formal audit —
					<code>kuyfi-report-&lt;reportId&gt;.pdf</code>
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Both</td>
				<td>TUI <code>[B]</code> / <code>--json --pdf</code></td>
				<td>Same <code>report_export.ts</code> helpers</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<ul>
		<li>
			All writes use Node <code>flag: 'wx'</code> — refuse to overwrite. Message:
			<code>Refusing to overwrite existing file: &lt;name&gt;</code>.
		</li>
		<li>
			TUI <code>exportSecurityReport('json'|'pdf'|'both')</code>: each format is
			attempted independently — a PDF failure does not delete a successful JSON file
			(and vice versa). Never throws; failures become outcome messages.
		</li>
		<li>
			CLI: any write failure (including EEXIST) → exit <code>1</code>. See
			<a href={withBase('/cli')}>CLI reference</a>.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<pre><code>kuyfi C… --json --pdf
# writes SecurityReport JSON + PDF from the identical object</code></pre>

	<h2 id="ci">CI semantics</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Gate parsers on <code>schemaVersion === "1.0.0"</code>.</li>
		<li>
			Process exit <code>0</code> with CRITICAL findings is <strong>expected</strong>
			— findings ≠ tool failure.
		</li>
		<li>
			Do not auto-fail pipelines as “CVE confirmed” on <code>POTENTIAL_VULN</code>
			alone — treat as investigate-first signal.
		</li>
	</ul>
</DocsLayout>
